# No local vault / personal machine details in git artifacts

PRs, commit messages, issue comments, and CHANGELOG entries are public. Do not include:

- Absolute home paths (`/home/<you>/…`, `/Users/<you>/…`, Windows profiles)
- OS usernames, machine hostnames, or vault paths (`/mnt/…`, Obsidian vault roots)
- Concrete local session filenames, project cards, or screenshots from a personal vault
- Examples that embed a real username — use placeholders: `/home/USER/…`, `<vault>`, `<user>`

Prefer generic wording in test plans ("build a vault with Claude sessions") over naming a specific local vault or rebuilt path.

`raw/` redaction to `USER` exists so committed transcripts stay anonymous — do not undo that privacy in PR text.
